From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:57:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: vp9: Keep the pool on downstream renegotiation

When downstream requests a reconfiguration while the decoder is
streaming, the base class calls negotiate() again. The decoder takes
its "Ignore downstream renegotiation request" path there, but still
chains up, and decide_allocation() allocates a second set of OUTPUT and
CAPTURE buffers while the first set is still in the streaming queues.
With a sink that asks for 8 buffers, the CAPTURE queue runs into the
VB2 limit of 32 buffers and decoding fails with "Not enough memory to
allocate source buffers".

Keep the current allocation while streaming as long as the allocators
are in place, as the H.264, H.265, MPEG-2 and VP8 decoders do.
negotiate() resets the allocation on a format change, so an
inter-frame resolution change still gets new buffers. The check was
dropped with commit e13065b22a ("v4l2codecs: vp9: Allow inter-frames
resolution change").

Link: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/merge_requests/13069
---
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecvp9dec.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecvp9dec.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecvp9dec.c
@@ -611,6 +611,10 @@ gst_v4l2_codec_vp9_dec_decide_allocation
   guint num_bitstream;
   gboolean has_videometa;
 
+  /* negotiate() only resets the allocation on a format change */
+  if (self->streaming && self->src_allocator)
+    goto no_internal_changes;
+
   g_clear_object (&self->src_pool);
   g_clear_object (&self->src_allocator);
   g_clear_object (&self->sink_allocator);
@@ -680,6 +684,7 @@ gst_v4l2_codec_vp9_dec_decide_allocation
   self->src_pool =
       gst_v4l2_codec_pool_new (self->src_allocator, &self->vinfo_drm);
 
+no_internal_changes:
   /* Our buffer pool is internal, we will let the base class create a video
    * pool, and use it if we are running out of buffers or if downstream does
    * not support GstVideoMeta */
